    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1427">

                <pb facs="1100" n="984" xml:id="pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/110.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Vice Consul Bevan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 744.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch,
                    No. 1316, dated December 12, 1914, with reference to forced contributions in the
                    Tuxpam oil district.</p>
                <p>Under date of December 24, 1914, the Department telegraphed to the American
                    Consul at Vera Cruz, referring to your report and directing him to request
                    Carranza to send a force sufficient to protect the companies in question from
                    this imposition.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilbur J. Carr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
